.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-EJECT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-eject
.Nd unmount removable media that is still plugged in
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar device | Ar mountpoint
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
unmounts a volume
.Xr novi-mount 8
mounted, flushes it, and is safe to run before pulling the device out.
.Pp
It
.Sy refuses
a busy mount rather than detaching the tree underneath it.
That is the entire difference between this and
.Nm novi-mount remove :
.Cm remove
runs when the device is already gone, where a plain unmount would
block on writeback to hardware that is not there, so it is lazy.
.Nm
runs while the device is still present, where
.Dq busy
means a program is genuinely still writing, and losing that data is
exactly what the command exists to prevent.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It exits non-zero if the volume is in use, naming what is holding it.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ novi-eject /run/media/PHOTOS
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr system.conf 5 ,
.Xr novi-mount 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0023.
